        "githubCommitMessage": "Install Vercel Web Analytics\n\n# Vercel Web Analytics Implementation\n\nSuccessfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this static HTML website.\n\n## Implementation Details\n\nThis project is a static HTML website (no build system or package manager), so I implemented Vercel Web Analytics using the HTML5/vanilla JavaScript approach as per the official Vercel documentation.\n\n### Changes Made\n\n**Added Vercel Analytics script to 7 key HTML pages:**\n\n1. `index.html` - Main landing page\n2. `games.html` - Games listing page  \n3. `class.html` - Class session page\n4. `admin.html` - Admin page\n5. `settings.html` - Settings page\n6. `search.html` - Search page\n7. `t9os.html` - T9OS page\n\n**Implementation approach:**\n\nFor each page, I added the following code in the `<head>` section immediately after the `<title>` tag:\n\n```html\n<script>\n    window.va = window.va || function () { (window.vaq = window.vaq || []).push(arguments); };\n</script>\n<script defer src=\"/_vercel/insights/script.js\"></script>\n```\n\nThis foll",
